{
  "id": "Compound::DB01069 - Gene::1128",
  "verbalization": "Promethazine is likely to interact with Chrm1 through a series of molecular and cellular mechanisms involving Hrh4. The evidence suggests that Promethazine binds to Hrh4, which then participates in receptor activity that is associated with Chrm1. This connection is supported by the shared participation of Hrh4 in different receptor-related activities, including G-protein coupled acetylcholine and neurotransmitter receptor activities, all of which are linked to Chrm1. The consistent involvement of Hrh4 in these pathways implies a potential role in mediating Promethazine's effects on Chrm1. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Promethazine influences Chrm1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
